# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange.py" "CO-CHANGE GATE: PASS" "co-change (logical coupling) extractor" "co-change (logical-coupling) extractor: the EMPIRICAL coupling signal that COMPLEMENTS the static code graph -- two files that keep changing together are coupled even when NO call/import/schema/config edge links them. It is a SECOND, INDEPENDENT detector next to the structural graph. CONTENT-FREE by construction: only file PATHS, per-commit grouping, and counts leave the repo -- never a line of code, commit message, author, or SHA. PRECISION-FIRST: giant refactor/merge/mass-format commits are skipped; strength is directional conditional probability; a support floor drops coincidental once-seen pairs; a strength floor stays silent below it. Proven deterministically on a synthetic git repository." "co-change extractor: empirical file coupling from git history, content-free + precision-disciplined (giant-commit skip, conditional probability, support floor)" 24
